ions to deal with the practice of profits or royalties being diverted to other jurisdictions that have lower or zero tax rates. For example, internet giant Alphabet Inc.'s ( GOOGL) Google paid a negligible amount as tax in the United Kingdom by completing its transactions in the low tax capital city of Dublin, Ireland, even though the revenue of $6.5 billion was earned in the UK. Mainly technology giants from the U.S., like Facebook Inc. ( FB), Apple Inc. ( AAPL) and Amazon.com Inc. ( AMZN), and other multinational corporations (MNC) like Starbucks Inc. ( SBUX) and Diageo PLC, have been using such practices to lower their tax bills.", "external_links": ["https://www.tumblr.com/widgets/share/tool?posttype=link&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investopedia.com%2Fterms%2Fg%2Fgoogle-tax.asp%3Fpartner%3DYahooSA%26yptr%3Dyahoo%26soc_src%3Dsocial-sh%26soc_trk%3Dtu&content=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investopedia.com%2Fterms%2Fg%2Fgoogle-tax.asp%3Fpartner%3DYahooSA%26yptr%3Dyahoo%26soc_src%3Dsocial-sh%26soc_trk%3Dtu&caption=A%20Google%20tax%2C%20also%20known%20as%20a%C2%A0diverted%20profits%20tax%2C%20refers%20to%20anti-avoidance%20tax%20provisions%20that%20have%20been%20introduced%20"], "published": "2018-09-05T16:44:00.000+03:00", "crawled": "2018-09-05T19:27:24.002+03:00", "highlightTitle": ""}